  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "On raising the temperature of the semiconductor, covalent bonds start breaking up and thus&nbsp;more charge carriers release. This will increase the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> and as a result the rate of collision of charge carriers will increase. This will decrease the drift speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>.",
